{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed for review: Gerrit change 1772 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1772), commit a520ba68d52.\n\nScope as certified: src/rebar/_store/push_recovery.py (+ a pure extraction in _store/sync.py) and new tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py. _recover_dirty_merge now runs _retry_untracked_overwrite between the failed post-stash merge and the abort net: parse abort-named paths with the shared sync parser (_untracked_overwrite_paths, pure), quarantine-move the named UNTRACKED paths, retry ONCE; anything else keeps today's behavior byte-for-byte. Stash ordering preserved — quarantine+retry sit between the failed merge and _restore_stash, and the stash commit is restored exactly once on every exit path (pinned by call-count tests).\n\nReuse boundary implemented as planned: the parser is imported from sync; the quarantine PATH arithmetic was extracted into a new pure sync._quarantine_dir_under(common, tracker) (sync._quarantine_dir now delegates to it) so push_recovery shares the dir shape (<git-common-dir>/reconverge-quarantine/<utc-ts>/) while its MOVER (_quarantine_untracked_paths) runs every git call through the late-bound core._git seam — sync's mover is never called across the seam, so the ~25 push._git monkeypatch sites keep working. The mover fences ALL named paths on git status --porcelain -uall '??' before moving anything (a mis-parse must never relocate tracked data) and refuses on an unresolvable common dir or a vanished path.\n\nDiscovery — _merge_remote_under_lock sibling seam needs NO code change: _DIRTY_WD (push_classify) matches 'would be overwritten by merge', so the untracked abort already routes into _recover_dirty_merge (stash create returns '' on a tree whose only change is untracked); a routing test (test_merge_remote_under_lock_routes_untracked_collision_to_recovery) pins that end-to-end.\n\nTDD: RED proof against pre-fix HEAD — the wedge test fails with _recover_dirty_merge returning False (merge aborted, origin not merged); 5 of 6 initial tests RED, the genuine-conflict guard green by design. GREEN: 8/8. Mutation pass: 13 mutants (never retry, invert detection, skip abort-before-move, skip move, invert '??' fence, ignore common-dir failure, DELETE instead of move, retry twice, drop/double stash restore, skip exists-check) — 11 killed by the fixture tests, 2 initial survivors (empty common dir ignored; exists-check skipped) killed by added fake-git degenerate-branch tests. All 13 killed.\n\nValidation: make lint clean, make typecheck clean (539 files), complexity ratchet active=53 new=0 increased=0, push_recovery.py 437 LOC / sync.py 406 LOC (cap 800). Full unit suite: 10272 passed; the 9 fails + 9 errors are the identical environmental set already reproduced on CLEAN HEAD during the wolverine session (ref_lock roundtrip, dirty_tracker delivery, sync_remote_config e2e pushes, bridge_provider matrix, push_pending_marker hooksPath) — none introduced. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1; ticket close deferred to the parent session per policy."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786695850775446001,"uuid":"f0f278fb-7bcb-4be8-99da-a9ca8072fcd4"}